          "name": "What does the customs factory inspection actually check?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Customs officers verify 12 items per the official Dongguan Customs photo standard (2026): packaging appearance (45 angle), UN marking dimensions (with ruler), hazard label dimensions, box length/width/height (with ruler at zero gap), seal method, gross weight (electronic scale, no glare), inner box with lithium batteries, cushioning material thickness, inner box product info face, net weight, product model/voltage/capacity label, and packaging performance test label. All factory-submitted photos must match on-site reality exactly, using the same angle, ruler, and scale as the filed application."
